# PS4 dialogue font table (16x16, 1bpp) - glyph table at $2A3452
#
# Separate from ps4.tbl, which covers the 8x8 bank used for names, battle text
# and item descriptions. The dialogue font is richer: voiced kana are
# PRE-COMPOSED here, so it needs no $F0/$F1 combining marks.
#
# Encoding (renderer $06AE1E, selector $06A9FA):
#   $00-$DF  single byte, index into this table
#   $E0-$EF  two bytes, (b0<<8|b1) & $0FFF -> kanji table at $1F62BA
#   $F0-$FF  control code, 16 handlers dispatched from $06AEA6
#
# Layout read directly off the rendered glyphs; indices run 0-209, and index
# 210+ is graphics. The script's single-byte codes top out at 208, exactly the
# last valid character, which corroborates both the table and the region.

# Control names are deliberately non-hex so they cannot be confused with
# {XX} raw-byte escapes. $FF ends a message, $FC breaks a line; the rest
# are dispatched from $06AEA6 but not yet identified.
*FF=END
*FC=BR
*F0=ctl.F0
*F1=ctl.F1
*F2=ctl.F2
*F3=ctl.F3
*F4=ctl.F4
*F5=ctl.F5
*F6=ctl.F6
*F7=ctl.F7
*F8=ctl.F8
*F9=ctl.F9
*FA=ctl.FA
*FB=ctl.FB
*FD=ctl.FD
*FE=ctl.FE

